he cache time is expired\n        if (\n            '://' not in inv_location\n            or project.target_uri not in cache\n            or cache[project.target_uri][1] < cache_time\n        ):\n            LOGGER.info(\n                __(\"loading intersphinx inventory '%s' from %s ...\"),\n                project.name,\n                _get_safe_url(inv_location),\n            )\n\n            try:\n                raw_data, target_uri = _fetch_inventory_data(\n                    target_uri=project.target_uri,\n                    inv_location=inv_location,\n                    config=config,\n                    srcdir=srcdir,\n                    cache_path=cache_path,\n                )\n                inv = _load_inventory(raw_data, target_uri=target_uri)\n            except Exception as err:\n                failures.append(err.args)\n                continue\n            else:\n                cache[project.target_uri] = project.name, now, inv.data\n                updated = True\n                break\n\n    if not failures:\n        pass\n    elif len(failures) < len(project.locations):\n        LOGGER.info(\n            __(\n                'encountered some issues with some of the inventories,'\n                ' but they had working alternatives:'\n            )\n        )\n        for fail in failures:\n            LOGGER.info(*fail)\n    else:\n        LOGGER.warning(\n            __('failed to reach any of the inventories with the following issues:\\n%s'),\n            _display_failures(failures),\n        )\n    return updated\n```\n\nFacts extracted from this version by a parser (tree-sitter):\nsignature: _fetch_inventory_group(project, cache, now, config, srcdir, cache_dir) -> bool\ncalls: LOGGER.info, LOGGER.warning, __, _display_failures, _fetch_inventory_data, _get_safe_url, _load_inventory, cache_path.is_file, cache_path.read_bytes, cache_path.stat, failures.append, int, len, posixpath.join\nreturn statements: return updated\nraise statem